<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-AW2R9-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-AW2R9-001" ;
  triage:title "AC3 non-interference (concurrent primary ops unaffected by diagnostic channel full/failing) has zero test coverage" ;
  triage:description "qa-pr1179-r9 (feature/aw2-sqlite-diagnostic-timeline @ 1d43815c6): req-qa: sprint doc AC3 (docs/plans/phase-aw/sprint-AW.2-sqlite-diagnostic-timeline.md:108-111) requires that concurrent send/read/ack/mailbox-write operations complete unaffected while the diagnostic channel is full or RecordDiagnostics is forced to fail. The only ac3_-named test (diagnostic_timeline.rs:501 ac3_diagnostic_persistence_failure_does_not_poison_later_offers) only verifies the diagnostic writer's own internal drop-counter/recovery bookkeeping under a mock store forced to fail; it never drives a concurrent real primary-path operation (send/read/ack/mailbox write) and asserts its result/latency is unaffected. quality-mgr independently confirmed by reading the test body: it takes no primary-path action at all. This is a genuine, previously-mistracked gap: an earlier record (AW2-QA-I2) mislabeled this criterion as 'AC4' due to an AC-numbering drift against an older draft of the sprint doc; the current doc's real AC3/AC4 order was independently confirmed via direct grep of the sprint doc's AC1-AC11 headings." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-coverage" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T07:05:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AW2 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-05T07:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-AW2R9-001/AW2-1> ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-05T07:20:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

# CLOSURE (qa-pr1179-r10, quality-mgr): arch-ctm's fix (494f7c31a) adds
# ac3_primary_mailbox_insert_completes_while_diagnostic_lane_is_full
# (crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/writer/mod.rs:1029). quality-mgr
# independently confirmed this drives the real production selector,
# receive_next_work (writer/mod.rs:564, the exact function the live writer
# loop calls at writer/mod.rs:526) -- it fills the real bounded
# tokio::sync::mpsc diagnostic channel to capacity (DIAGNOSTIC_QUEUE_BATCHES),
# confirms it is Full via try_send, then admits a real primary mailbox
# WriterMessage::Submit concurrently and asserts receive_next_work still
# selects and completes it (UpsertMessage inserted=true, row persisted via a
# real SELECT COUNT(*) against mail_messages). This is a genuine
# non-interference test against the real channel/selector, not a mock.
# cargo test -p atm-storage-rusqlite -p atm-daemon-bootstrap: 133 passed, 0
# failed, no regressions. Note: this push does not address AW2-QA-I2 (AC7's
# PausedTimeline mock is unchanged at diagnostic_timeline.rs:425) -- that
# finding remains separately open.

